\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qc\kerning2\b\f0\fs32 LangChain, LlamaIndex and Haystack\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Introduction to AI Frameworks\lang16393\~\par
\b0\fs24\lang1033 Generative AI applications require orchestration frameworks that connect Large Language Models (LLMs) with external data, business processes, APIs, and enterprise systems. LangChain, LlamaIndex, and Haystack are among the most popular open-source frameworks used for building Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), AI agents, chatbots, enterprise search solutions, and intelligent assistants. These frameworks simplify development by providing reusable components for prompt management, memory, retrieval, indexing, and workflow automation.\lang16393\~\line\~\line\lang1033 Organizations use these frameworks to build customer support bots, knowledge management systems, document analysis platforms, and autonomous AI agents.\lang16393\~\par
\lang1033 Generative AI applications require orchestration frameworks that connect Large Language Models (LLMs) with external data, business processes, APIs, and enterprise systems. LangChain, LlamaIndex, and Haystack are among the most popular open-source frameworks used for building Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), AI agents, chatbots, enterprise search solutions, and intelligent assistants. These frameworks simplify development by providing reusable components for prompt management, memory, retrieval, indexing, and workflow automation.\lang16393\~\line\~\line\lang1033 Organizations use these frameworks to build customer support bots, knowledge management systems, document analysis platforms, and autonomous AI agents.\lang16393\par
\lang1033\par
\b\fs28 LangChain\lang16393\~\fs24\par
\b0\lang1033 LangChain is an open-source framework used to build LLM-powered applications. It provides components such as prompts, chains, agents, memory, and tools that help developers connect language models with external systems and data sources.\lang16393\~\par

